command, runtime_file: a launch's Auto save slot survives content load

ROCKNIX's launcher writes state_slot = "-1" -- RetroArch's Auto slot,
the .state.auto file -- into a launch's append config for a game started
from its auto save, so that the load-state hotkey reloads the state the
player launched with. Two things replaced it before the game's first
frame:

- command_event_set_savestate_auto_index() ran at every content load
  and set the slot to the highest numbered one it could find (0 when
  there is none, logged as "found_last_state_slot: #0"), or to 0
  outright with savestate_auto_index off.
- runtime_log_init() restored the slot the game was last left on from
  the runtime log (runtime_file.c), through runloop_st->entry_state_slot,
  which runloop.c then applies -- so a game left on slot 0 came back on
  slot 0 whatever this launch had asked for.

So the hotkey built its path from slot 0 and loaded a file that does not
exist -- "[State] Loading state ".../mspacman.state", 0 bytes. / Failed
to load state" on an RG35XX SP, 2026-09-25, after a launch whose append
config carried state_slot = "-1"; and again on the QA guest with the
first half alone patched (2026-09-26), where the log's remembered 0 was
the second half. With both halves, on the QA guest (image a8175c6193,
2026-09-26): no found_last_state_slot line, and the load-state key --
sent through the guest's monitor, not a pad -- loaded Probe.state.auto.

Both leave the slot alone only when this launch's append config sets it
negative, and say so in the log. The answer is taken when the
configuration loads: config_load_file hands command.c the --appendconfig
list right after appending its files, and the last file that sets
state_slot wins, as it does in the load -- so the answer describes the
files RetroArch read, not whatever is at those paths by the time content
loads, and a file that cannot be read says nothing. A -1 that reached
the main config instead -- a configuration saved while Auto was
selected -- is not this launch's request: it is scanned, reset or
restored over as upstream does, so a launch that asks for no slot
behaves as it always has.

diff --git a/command.c b/command.c
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -1903,6 +1903,60 @@ int command_event_get_next_savestate_auto_index(settings_t *settings)
    return new_state_slot;
 }
 
+/* ROCKNIX: append auto slot begin */
+/* Whether a launch's append config (--appendconfig, where ROCKNIX's
+ * launcher writes one launch's settings) asks for RetroArch's Auto slot,
+ * the .state.auto file. The answer is taken when the configuration is
+ * loaded -- config_load_file hands the list over right after appending its
+ * files -- so it describes the files RetroArch read, not whatever is at
+ * those paths by the time content loads. A negative that reached the main
+ * config instead (a configuration saved while Auto was selected) is not a
+ * launch's request and does not count. */
+static bool command_append_auto_slot = false;
+
+/* The '|'-separated list read as RetroArch reads it: the last file that
+ * sets state_slot wins; a file that cannot be read, or has no state_slot,
+ * says nothing. True when the winning value is negative. */
+bool command_append_list_sets_auto_slot(const char *list)
+{
+   char tmp[PATH_MAX_LENGTH];
+   char *ptr    = NULL;
+   bool is_auto = false;
+
+   if (!list || !*list)
+      return false;
+
+   strlcpy(tmp, list, sizeof(tmp));
+   for (ptr = tmp; ptr && *ptr; )
+   {
+      char *delim         = strchr(ptr, '|');
+      config_file_t *conf = NULL;
+      int slot            = 0;
+
+      if (delim)
+         *delim = '\0';
+      if (*ptr && (conf = config_file_new_from_path_to_string(ptr)))
+      {
+         if (config_get_int(conf, "state_slot", &slot))
+            is_auto = (slot < 0);
+         config_file_free(conf);
+      }
+      ptr = delim ? delim + 1 : NULL;
+   }
+   return is_auto;
+}
+
+void command_record_append_config(const char *list)
+{
+   command_append_auto_slot = command_append_list_sets_auto_slot(list);
+}
+
+bool command_append_config_sets_auto_slot(void)
+{
+   return command_append_auto_slot;
+}
+/* ROCKNIX: append auto slot end */
+
 /**
  * Determines most recent savestate slot in case of content load.
  *
@@ -1913,6 +1967,18 @@ void command_event_set_savestate_auto_index(settings_t *settings)
 {
    unsigned max_idx          = 0;
    bool savestate_auto_index = settings->bools.savestate_auto_index;
+   /* ROCKNIX: the launcher sets state_slot = -1 in this launch's append
+    * config for a game started from its auto save, so that the load-state
+    * hotkey reloads the state the player launched with; resetting it here
+    * to 0, or to the last numbered slot, sent that hotkey to a slot 0 file
+    * that does not exist. That Auto is left alone. Any other slot -- a
+    * numbered one, or a -1 saved into the main config -- is scanned or
+    * reset as upstream does. */
+   if (settings->ints.state_slot < 0 && command_append_config_sets_auto_slot())
+   {
+      RARCH_LOG("[State] Keeping the Auto slot this launch's configuration asks for.\n");
+      return;
+   }
    if (savestate_auto_index)
    {
       command_scan_states(
